.TH CHTTPSVR_CONSTRUCT_SCOPED 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_construct_scoped \- declare a chttpsvr handle, initialize it, and destroy it automatically
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

chttpsvr_construct_scoped(name, cl);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Combines chttpsvr_declare_scoped with a call to
ccol_create_chttpsvr(cl).  It declares name with a GCC cleanup
attribute, so the server is destroyed automatically, exactly as
chttpsvr_destroy would destroy it, when name goes out of scope.  On
failure the macro calls ccol_fatal_err() and does not return.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
name     The identifier for the new handle variable.
cl       The parent logger from which the logger of this server is
         derived.  Pass CLOG_INVALID to use an internal logger that
         writes only FATAL messages to stderr; see
         ccol_create_chttpsvr_mp for details.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_construct (3),
.BR chttpsvr_declare_scoped (3)
